      "writtenOn": "2023-08-22T16:22:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `drivers.defauilt.*` tests are probably just failing due to a timing change. Reaching into the state machines and checking their internal state isn\u0027t a great way to write a test, but sometimes it\u0027s all we have to assert on. You might just need to tweak a sleep in the test.\n\nIt wouldn\u0027t terribly surprise me if the other tests are being affected in a similar way. `verify_no_vconn_swap` is a little more concerning. The implementation of the policy this test is verifying is at https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/main/common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c#3739, and that flags is checked at https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/main/common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c#889. Running without this change, you should be able to hit breakpoints/prints at those locations and see that it\u0027s working. You\u0027re right that your change shouldn\u0027t affect that, so you might need to debug into the test run.",
      "parentUuid": "18529aaf_f864f53f",
      "revId": "a566435852c504ece63884c049413dfad23a2964",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
