      "side": 1,
      "message": "Seems like the entire line `(pd_capable(port) || pd_waiting_on_partner_src_caps(port))` should be removed, as when the first condition is true the second condition is false, and vice versa. There is a (theoretical) possibility that a the partner is not pd capable but reported src caps, but I assume this is an bad state and we should not make muxing decisions based on it.\n\nLeaving only the `pd_capable(port)` condition (as in patchset 5) allowed the USB3 lines to be connected if the partner is not pd capable, and the failed tests were reflecting that erroneous decision.",
